# Line-ending policy for files whose bytes flow into generated artifacts.
#
# templates/*.md are XOR-encrypted verbatim (byte-for-byte) into
# src/prompt/prompt_encrypted.rs by scripts/encrypt_templates.py, and the CI
# drift gate regenerates + diffs that artifact. If checkout normalizes these
# files' line endings differently on different platforms, the encrypted array
# diverges and the gate fails on one OS. Pin both sides to CRLF — the current
# committed bytes — so every checkout yields identical bytes everywhere.
crates/codegen/cf-agent/templates/*.md text eol=crlf
crates/codegen/cf-agent/src/prompt/prompt_encrypted.rs text eol=crlf

# cf-shell goal templates flow through include_str! into rendered text whose
# newline bytes are pinned by tests (line-anchored assertions). The repo
# stores them as LF; pin checkout to LF everywhere so Windows include_str!
# bytes match the Linux CI bytes.
crates/codegen/cf-shell/src/session/templates/*.md text eol=lf